{"raw": {"https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CHI/2026/Oct/chi_ap_pt_2026-10-05.pdf": {"title": "Part-time Lecturer", "description": "\u9999\u6e2f\u6a39\u4ec1\u5927\u5b78\u4e2d\u570b\u8a9e\u8a00\u6587\u5b78\u7cfb\u64ec\u62db\u8058\u517c\u8077\u8b1b\u5e2b\uff08\u591a\u540d\uff09\uff0c\u9700\u65bc 2027 \u5e74 1 \u6708\u5230\u8077\uff0c\n\u61c9\u5fb5\u689d\u4ef6\u5982\u4e0b\uff1a  \n \n1\u3001\u64c1\u6709\u4e2d\u570b\u8a9e\u8a00\u53ca\u6587\u5b78\u6216\u76f8\u95dc\u7684\u78a9\u58eb\u6216\u535a\u58eb\u5b78\u4f4d\uff1b \n2\u3001\u52dd\u4efb\u6559\u6388\u300c\u5927\u4e00\u570b\u6587\u300d (\u5167\u5bb9\u5305\u62ec\u6587\u8a00\u6587\u7bc7\u7ae0\u3001\u61c9\u7528\u6587\u53ca\u5275\u610f\u5beb\u4f5c)\uff1b \n3\u3001\u6709\u8207\u4e2d\u6587\u7814\u7a76\u76f8\u95dc\u7684\u5b78\u8853\u51fa\u7248\u7d00\u9304\u3002 \n\u53d7\u8058\u8077\u7d1a\u8207\u7533\u8acb\u8005\u4e4b\u5b78\u8853\u80cc\u666f\u76f8\u7b26\u3002 \n\u85aa\u916c\u9762\u8b70 \n\u9644\u8a3b\uff1a  \n1. \u8acb\u4e0b\u8f09\u4e26\u586b\u5beb\u7533\u8acb\u8868\uff0c\u53e6\u9644\u500b\u4eba\u7c21\u6b77\uff1b  \n2. \u8acb\u9644\u4e0a\u5b78\u4f4d\u8b49\u66f8\u3001\u8077\u696d\u8cc7\u683c\u8b49\u66f8\u3001\u7372\u734e\u8b49\u66f8\uff08\u82e5\u6709\uff09\u4e4b\u985e\u8b49\u660e\u6587\u4ef6\u7684\u6383\u63cf\u7248\u6216  \n\u5f71\u5370\u672c\uff1b  \n3. \u63d0\u4f9b\u5169\u4f4d\u5177\u6559\u6388\u8077\u7a31\uff08\u5305\u62ec\u52a9\u7406\u6559\u6388\u3001\u526f\u6559\u6388\u53ca\u6b63\u6559\u6388\uff09\u7684\u5c08\u5bb6\u63a8\u85a6\u4fe1\u3002 \n \n\u96fb\u90f5\u81f3\uff1akylam@hksyu.edu\uff08\u90f5\u4ef6\u4e3b\u984c\uff1a\u61c9\u5fb5\u517c\u8077\u6559\u8077\uff09  \n\u6216\u90f5\u5bc4\u81f3\uff1a\u9999\u6e2f\u6a39\u4ec1\u5927\u5b78\u4e2d\u570b\u8a9e\u8a00\u6587\u5b78\u7cfb\uff08\u4fe1\u5c01\u4e0a\u8acb\u8a3b\u660e\uff1a\u61c9\u5fb5\u6559\u8077\uff09  \n\u622a\u6b62\u62db\u8058\u671f\uff1a2026 \u5e74 12 \u6708 1 \u65e5\u6216\u8a72\u8077\u4f4d\u88ab\u586b\u88dc\u70ba\u6b62\uff08\u9074\u9078\u7a0b\u5e8f\u5c07\u65bc\u6536\u5230\u7533\u8acb\u6750\n\u6599\u5373\u6642\u958b\u59cb\uff09 \n\u8aee\u8a62\u8acb\u806f\u7e6b\u6797\u5c0f\u59d0\uff0c\u96fb\u8a71\uff1a28065191\uff0c\u50b3\u771f 28068044\u3002 \n\u7533\u8acb\u8005\u5c07\u65bc\u905e\u4ea4\u5168\u90e8\u6240\u9700\u6750\u6599\u4e09\u9031\u5167\u7372\u9080\u9762\u8a66\u3002\u60df\u5165\u9078\u9762\u8a66\u8005\u65b9\u7372\u767c\u901a\u77e5 \u3002\u6240\u6709\n\u7533\u8acb\u8cc7\u6599\u53ea\u4f5c\u62db\u8058\u4e4b\u7528\u3002 \n \nPart-time Lecturer \nPart-time Academic Positions in Chinese Language and Literature (January 2027)  \n  \nThe Department of Chinese Language and Literature invites applications for part-time \nLecturer in teaching the course \u201cFirst Year Chinese\u201d (multiple posts). Applicants should:  \n(i) possess a doctorate in Chinese language and literature or related disciplines. \n(ii) be capable of teaching \u201cFirst Year Chinese\u201d  (teaching content includes classical \nChinese literature, practical writing and creative writing).  \n(iii) have relevant publications. \n \nSalary: To be negotiated according to academic qualifications and teaching experience. \n \nFurther details of the Department and its programme are located at \nhttps://chinese.hksyu.edu/. For enquiries, please contact Ms. Lam  via e -mail: \nkylam@hksyu.edu. \n \nClosing Date: December 1, 2026, or the posts are filled \nInformation about the Department and its programme are located at \nhttps://chinese.hksyu.edu/. For queries about the application process, please contact \nMs. Lam via e-mail: kylam@hksyu.edu. \n \nApplication Procedure  \n  \nApplicants should download and fill out the application form from the University \nwebsite, and attach the following materials: \n1. complete curriculum vitae;  \n2. copies of qualification documents;  \n3. two recommendation letters from relevant experts  in Chinese Language and \nLiterature. \nApplication materials should be sent to the following address or by email:   \nMs. Lam, Administrative Assistant, Department of Chinese Language and Literature, \nHong Kong Shue Yan University,   \n10 Wai Tsui Crescent, Braemar Hill, Hong Kong  \n(The envelope should be marked \u201cApplication for part-time academic position\u201d) \nEmail: kylam@hksyu.edu (The subject should be indicated \u201cApplication for academic \nposition\u201d) \nReview of applications will start immediately. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted \nwithin three weeks of receipt of complete application. Personal data collected will be \nused for staff recruitment purposes only. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/JC/2026/May/jc_ap_digicomm_ft_2026-05-27.pdf": {"title": "Full-time Academic Position in Digital Communication", "description": "Full-time Academic Position in Digital Communication \nDepartment of Journalism and Communication, Hong Kong Shue Yan University \n \nThe Department of Journalism and Communication is inviting applications for the post \nof Full-time Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Associate Professor of Practice / \nProfessor of Practice / Professor in Digital Communication.  \n \nRank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Candidates of Assistant \nProfessor/Associate Professor/Professor should have a doctorate degree in \ncommunication or a related discipline . Recognized professionals with substantial years \nof experience who have made significant contributions to the professional field in terms \nof practice and education of the profession could be considered as Associate Professor \nof Practice / Professor of Practice.  \n \nCandidates should demonstrate abilities to teach effectively at the undergraduate level \nwhile pursuing an active research agenda in at least one, but preferably more of the \nfollowing areas: \n1. Digital advertising  \n2. Digital public relations  \n3. Digital media communication \n \nPreference will be given to applicants with substantial tertiary-level teaching experience \nand an established track record in research and publication. The c apability of teaching \nhands-on skills using artificial intelligence and/or digital technology is also an advantage. \n \nThe appointment is contract-based, commencing in Academic Year 2026/27 and \nrenewable upon mutual agreement. \n \nApplication Procedure: \nApplicants should apply by sending: \n(1) a cover letter; \n(2) a statement of teaching and research; \n(3) a complete CV (including a list of publications); \n(4) three representative publications; \n(5) three references to be sent directly from the referees; and \n(6) the application form which can be downloaded from : \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nPlease submit your application by send ing the required documents to  University \nSecretary via email recruit_ap@hksyu.edu. \nFor further information about the Department, please visit https://jc.hksyu.edu/en. \n \nApplication Deadline: \nReview of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted.  Personal data collected will be used for \nstaff recruitment purposes only. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/BA/2024/Aug/ba_ap_pt_ft_2024-08-12.pdf": {"title": "Full-time /Part-time Academic Position in Business Administration", "description": "Full-time /Part-time Academic Position in Business Administration \nDepartment of Business Administration \nThe Department of Business Administration invites applications for full - time/part-time \nLecturer/Senior Lecturer/Assistant Professor/Associate  Professor/Professor . \nApplicants should possess doctoral/master qualifications in relevant business discipline. \nFields of specialization include, but are not limited to human resource management, \ndigital marketing, applied business psychology, AI/IT business application s , and  \nbusiness analytics. \nApplicants should have a good command of both written and spoken English and \nChinese. Excellent communication skills and the ability to use Putonghua and \nSimplified Chinese as the primary language of instruction will be highly advantageous. \nPreference will also be given to those applicants who have at least two years of teaching \nexperience, a good track record in research and publication, and good academic and/or \nprofessional experience in teaching at the higher education level (bachelor and/or \nmaster). \nThe appointment is contract-based and renewable upon mutual agreement. Salary will \nbe commensurate with qualifications and experience. \nApplication Procedure \nApplicants should apply by sending: \n(1) a cover letter; \n(2) a s tatement of teaching and research; \n(3) a complete CV ( including  a  list of publications); \n(4) at least two representative publications (within recent 5 years); \n(5) three references to be sent directly from the referees; and \n(6) the application form which can be downloaded from \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ \nPlease send the above documents to the University Secretary via email \nrecruit_ap@hksyu.edu . For further information about the Department, please visit \nhttps://ba.hksyu.edu/. \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used for \nrecruitment purposes only. The posts  are open until filled and all applications will \nreceive full consideration.  \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SOC/2026/Sep/soc_ap_ft_2026-09-07.pdf": {"title": "is inviting applications for a full-time Assistant/Associate Professor position to start in", "description": "The Arts, Culture and Technology (ACT) Programme of the Department of Sociology \nis inviting applications for a full-time Assistant/Associate Professor position to start in \nJanuary 2027. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. \nCandidates should demonstrate the ability to effectively teach at the undergraduate \nlevel while pursuing an active research agenda. Candidates should possess a PhD \ndegree in Computer Engineering, 3D Imaging, VR/AR, Photogrammetry, or relevant \ndisciplines, and will be expected to make contributions to teaching and research in \nDigital Technology/3D Imaging.  The candidate will be expected to teach courses in \n3D data acquisition and processing, which may include  Terrestrial LiDAR scanning, \nDrone surveys, 3D close-range photogrammetry techniques and immersive applications \n(e.g., Unity, Unreal and Blender). Candidates with experience in the application of 3D \nimaging technology to the art, culture and heritage sectors will have an advantage. \nThe ACT programme seeks to bridge knowledge of arts and culture with digital \ninnovation. It delves into the dynamics of  how arts, culture and technology impact \nsociety, and vice versa. Faculty members of the ACT programme are expected to take \nan interdisciplinary approach to teaching and research,  \nPreference will be given to applicants who have at least two years of teaching \nexperience and a good track record in research and publication. Proficiency in English \nis required, while proficiency in Chinese will be an advantage.  \n \nApplications should be addressed to: Department of Sociology, Hong Kong Shue Yan \nUniversity, 10 Wai Tsui Crescent, North Point, Hong Kong; or via email to \nrecruit_ap@hksyu.edu. It should include: (1) cover letter; (2) complete CV including \nlist of research projects and publications ; (3) Teaching Statement  (250 words);  (4) \nResearch Statement  (250 words);  (5) two representative publications ; and ( 6) three \nreferences to be sent by the referees directly to the University. For further information \nabout the University and the Department of Sociology, please visit \nhttps://sociology.hksyu.edu/en; for enquires, please send email to soc@hksyu.edu.  \n \nThe Search Committee will begin reviewing applications on September  30, 2026 and \ncontinue until  the position is filled. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. \nPersonal data received will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purposes only.  \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/May/counpsy_ap_ft_2026-05-28.pdf": {"title": "Full-time Academic Position in Counselling Psychology", "description": "Full-time Academic Position in Counselling Psychology \n \nDepartment of Counselling and Psychology \nThe Department of Counselling and Psychology invites applications for full-time \nacademic positions. Applicants should hold a doctoral degree in Psychology or a related \nfield, along with relevant teaching and research experience. Experience in at least one, \npreferably more, of the following areas would be advantageous: \n\uf0b7 Criminal Psychology \n\uf0b7 Forensic Psychology \n\uf0b7 Investigative Psychology \n\uf0b7 Play Therapy \n\uf0b7 Trauma Psychology \n\uf0b7 Sport Psychology \n\uf0b7 Psychology of Exercise \n\uf0b7 Industrial and Organisational Psychology \n\uf0b7 Physical Therapy \nThe appointees are expected to provide research supervision to students at \nundergraduate and postgraduate levels. The academic rank offered will be \ncommensurate with the academic and/or clinical background and experience of the \nsuccessful candidate.  \n \nThe appointment is contract-based and renewable upon mutual agreement.  \n \nFurther details of the Department and its programmes are located at \nhttp://www.hksyu.edu/counpsy/. \n \nApplication Procedure \nApplicants should send a letter of application together with a completed application \nform, curriculum vitae, copies of qualification documents, three reference letters from \npeople who know your work, and one sample of your most recent publications to \nrecruit_ap@hksyu.edu \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data collected will be used for \nstaff recruitment purposes only. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Eng/2025/Feb/eng_lc_ft_2025-02-18.pdf": {"title": "Full-time Lecturer/Senior Lecturer Positions", "description": "Hong Kong Shue Yan University \nDepartment of English Language and Literature \nFull-time Lecturer/Senior Lecturer Positions \nThe Department of English Language and Literature invites applications for the posts of \nLecturer/Senior Lecturer. Applicants should have a doctoral degree in English or a related subject and \ndemonstrated ability to teach academic literacy and general English language skills effectively \nat the undergraduate level. Preference will be given to applicants with at least two years\u2019 tertiary \nlevel teaching experience.  \nLecturers will be expected to teach 18 hours per week and undertake research as well as \nundertaking administrative duties as assigned by the Department Head. \nSuitably qualified and experienced applicants could be considered for appointment at the rank \nof Senior Lecturer. \nThe application should contain a cover letter, a complete CV, a completed application form \n(available at the External Vacancies section of the University website at https://\nwww.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy) and three references  to be sent directly from \nthe referees to University Secretary via email recruit_ap@hksyu.edu. \nFor further information about the University please visit https://www.hksyu.edu/en/ and the \nDepartment of English Language and Literature website at https://english.hksyu.edu/. \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used for \nrecruitment purposes only.  \nThe position will remain open until filled. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Eng/2025/Feb/eng_ap_ft_2025-02-18.pdf": {"title": "Professor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor", "description": "Hong Kong Shue Yan University \nDepartment of English Language and Literature \nProfessor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor \nThe Department of English Language and Literature invites applications for the post \nof full-ti me Professor, Associate or Assistant Professor. Rank will be \ncommensurate with qualifications and experience. Candidates  should have a \ndoctoral degree in English specializing in literature, linguistics or a related \nfield and demonstrated ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and \npostgraduate levels while pursuing an active research agenda. Preference will be \ngiven to candidates with experience in research postgraduate supervision. \nSuccessful candidates may also be asked to contribute to the teaching of academic \nliteracy. Preference will be given to applicants with substantial tertiary level teaching \nexperience a nd an established t rack record in research a nd publication.  \nApplications  should  be addressed  to: The University Secretary , Hong Kong Shue Yan \nUniversity, 10 Wai Tsui Crescent, Braemar Hill, North Point, Hong Kong and sent by \nemail to recruit_ap@hksyu.edu. The application  should  contain  a cover letter, a \ncomplete  CV including  a list of publications, two representative  publications,  a \ncompleted  application  form (available  at the External  Vacancies  section  of the \nUniversity  website  at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external- vacancy ) and three \nreferences  to be sent directly  from the referees.   \nFor further information about   the University , please visit https://www.hksyu.edu/en/ \nand the Department of English Language and Literature website at \nhttps://english.hksyu.edu/. \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used \nfor recruitment purposes only. \nApplications should be submitted as soon as possible.   The position will remain open \nuntil filled. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Eng/2025/Jun/eng_lc_pt_2025-06-30.pdf": {"title": "Part-time Lecturer positions", "description": "June 2025  \nHong Kong Shue Yan University \nDepartment of English Language and Literature \n \nPart-time Lecturer positions \n \nThe Department of English Language and Literature invites applications for the posts of part- \ntime Lecturer. Applicants should have a recognized degree in English or a related subject and \ndemonstrated ability to teach academic literacy and general English language skills effectively \nat the undergraduate level. Preference will be given to applicants with a higher degree in \nEnglish or a related subject and at least two years\u2019 tertiary level teaching experience. \n \nThe application should contain a cover letter, a complete CV, and three references to be sent \ndirectly from the referees. The application may be submitted by email to english@hksyu.edu. \n \nFor further information about the University please visit https://www.hksyu.edu/en/ and the \nDepartment of English Language and Literature website https://english.hksyu.edu/. For other \nenquiries, please email english@hksyu.edu. \n \n \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used for \nrecruitment purposes only. \n \nApplications should be submitted as soon as possible. \nThe positions will remain open until filled. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SW/2026/Apr/ap_sw_fs_pt_2026-04-08.pdf": {"title": "Part-Time Fieldwork Supervisor", "description": "Part-Time Fieldwork Supervisor \n \nDepartment of Social Work is inviting applications for part-time Fieldwork Supervisor.  \n \nKey Responsibilities: \nThe successful candidate will be tasked with the following duties:  \n(i) Supervising social work students during their fieldwork placements;  \n(ii) Evaluating and grading students' assignments, as well as preparing \nsupervision records and related documentation;  \n(iii) Participating in meetings and trainings. \n \nQualifications: \nCandidates must satisfy the following criteria:  \n(i) Hold a recognized degree in social work and/or possession of a postgraduate \ndegree in social work or a related discipline;  \n(ii) Possess at least five years of full-time-equivalent post-degree professional \npractice experience (at a rank equivalent to ASWO); \n(iii) Demonstrate strong communication and interpersonal skills; \n(iv) Possess strong written and spoken English and Chinese skills. \n \nPlease note that we will conduct a short Zoom interview before the start of each annual \nplacement. These interviews are normally held between March and April and between \nJune and July. \nThe appointment is contract-based and renewable by mutual agreement for each \ncohort. Enquiries and applications should be sent to the Fieldwork Team at \nswfw_joint@hksyu.edu.  \nPlease indicate your supervision preference priority (e.g., 1st: BSW, \n2nd: MSW or vice versa) in both the email subject line and your CV. \nApplication Deadline \nUntil the position is filled \n \nPosting date: 8 April 2026 "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SW/2024/Apr/sw_coord_l_sl_pt_ft_2024-04-02.pdf": {"title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer / Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor", "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer / Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor \nDepartment of Social Work \n \nDepartment of Social Work is inviting applications for full -time Lecturer, Senior \nLecturer, Assistant Professor , Associate Professor  and Professor. Rank will \ncommensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \n\uf09f Requirements for Lecturer / Senior Lecturer: \nCandidates should have a master degree in social work or related disciplines, and \n5 years of clinical practice experience as a social worker. Preference will be given \nto applicants with at least two years of teaching experience at the undergraduate \nlevel and conducting fieldwork supervision. Applicants are expected to take up \nteaching task, fieldwork supervision and administrating task. \n \nApplications should contain (a) application form, (b) a cover letter, and (c) a \ncomplete CV. \n \n\uf09f Requirements for Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor: \nCandidates should have a doctorate degree in social work or related disciplines, \nand 5 years of clinical practice experience as a social worker. Preference will be \ngiven to applicants with at least two years of teaching experience at the \nundergraduate and postgraduate levels and a good track record in research and \npublication. Applicants are expected to pursue an active research agenda. \n \nFields of specialization could include, but not limited to, children and family; \nyouth work; digital social work practice; support for children with special needs; \nsocial service management; interdisciplinary collaboration; social policy and \nadvocacy. Proficiency in Chinese and English is required. \n \nApplications should contain (a) application form, (b) a cover letter, (c) a complete \nCV including list of publications, ( d) a sample of recent publications, and ( e) 3 \nreferences to be sent directly from the referees to the Executive Officer.  \nThe appointment is contract-based and renewable upon mutual agreement. \n \nEnquiry and application should be sent to the University Secretary at \nrecruit_ap@hksyu.edu. \n \nApplication Deadline \nDeadline: Open Until Filled \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal  data collected will be used for \nstaff recruitment purpose only. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/qess/2026/Jul/qess_ro_ft_2026-07-15.pdf": {"title": "Project Officer", "description": "Project Officer  \nHong Kong Shue Yan University is seeking a high-calibre Project Officer for the QESS-\nfunded project titled \u201cEnhancing Students\u2019 Emotional Wellness and Resilience in Post-\nsecondary Institutions.\u201d This initiative aims to strengthen student mental wellness and \nresilience through a multi-pronged approach featuring a dedicated online learning platform, \nan AI-powered consultation chatbot, and experiential wellness programs. \nMajor Duties & Responsibilities \n\u2022 Plan, implement, and monitor project activities to ensure timely, high-quality execution in \nline with milestones. \n\u2022 Design and conduct project evaluation studies, including survey design, data collection, \nrigorous data analysis, and reporting. \n\u2022 Prepare comprehensive progress reports, engaging presentations, and concise evaluation \nsummaries for stakeholders. \n\u2022 Organize and facilitate workshops, seminars, committee meetings, and training events to \nsupport project objectives. \n\u2022 Support student-led activities and oversee the Student Ambassador Program to promote \nmental wellness and resilience on campus. \n\u2022 Develop and design creative promotional materials, including posters, infographics, and \nengaging content for social media platforms. \n\u2022 Regularly update and maintain the project website and online learning platform to ensure \ncontent is current and accurate. \n\u2022 Act as a key point of contact to maintain seamless communication with partner \ninstitutions, external collaborators, Student Ambassadors, and technical vendors. \n\u2022 Maintain meticulous project documentation, track budgets, and prepare progress reports \nin compliance with funding and organizational standards. \nQualifications & Requirements \n\u2022 A Bachelor\u2019s degree or above in Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, IT \nManagement, or a related discipline. \n\u2022 Proven experience in project coordination, survey design, and data collection/analysis is \nhighly preferred. \n\u2022 Strong organizational, administrative, and interpersonal communication skills. \n\u2022 Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Cantonese). \n\u2022 A genuine passion for promoting student mental health, resilience, and well-being. \nApplication  \nInterested applicants should submit a completed application form (specifying expected \nsalary), alongside a cover letter and an up-to-date curriculum vitae to Dr Jason CHOW \n(tschow@hksyu.edu). The official application form can be downloaded at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ \nAll applications will be treated in strict confidence. Only shortlisted candidates will be \ncontacted. \nClosing Date: by 10 August 2026 or until the position is filled.   "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/OAVP/2026/May/oavp_ea_ft_2026-05-27.pdf": {"title": "Position: Full-time Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant I, Office of the", "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \nPosition: Full-time Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant I, Office of the \nAcademic Vice President  \n \nResponsibilities \n\uf06c To provide high-level administrative and secretarial support for the daily office operations, \nmeetings, committees, and events; \n\uf06c To coordinate meeting logistics, prepare agendas and papers, and produce accurate \nmeeting minutes; \n\uf06c To draft, review, and handle confidential correspondence, reports, and presentations; \n\uf06c To liaise with faculties, departments, and administrative units on academic matters and \nsubmissions; \n\uf06c To manage an effective filing system and database for records; \n\uf06c To provide assistance on University functions as required (e.g. Luncheon meeting; Staff \nForum); \n\uf06c To perform any other duties as assigned by the Academic Vice President.  \n \nRequirements \n\uf06c Bachelor\u2019s degree holder; \n\uf06c Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; \n\uf06c Possess initiative in handling different tasks with tight timelines; \n\uf06c Be able to work independently and efficiently in a fast-paced environment; \n\uf06c A team player with good interpersonal and communication skills; \n\uf06c Knowledge in basic webpage management skills and design preferred; \n\uf06c Salary will be commensurate with qualification and experience. \n \nCandidates with more relevant experience may be considered for appointment as Senior \nExecutive Assistant. \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form and resume to the Academic Vice President \n(via email: tytwong@hksyu.edu). The application form can be obtained at:  \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Application%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Positions.doc  \n \nReview of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/APDO/2026/Sep/apdo_ea_ft_2026-09-17.pdf": {"title": "Position: Executive Assistant, Accreditation and Programme Development Office (APDO)", "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \n \nPosition: Executive Assistant, Accreditation and Programme Development Office (APDO) \n \nResponsibilities \n\uf06c To provide administrative and secretarial support for accreditation exercises, quality assurance \n(QA) mechanisms and programme development initiatives; \n\uf06c To liaise with academic and administrative units in the preparation of programme accreditation, \nreview and development activities; \n\uf06c To assist in the compilation, editing and maintenance of data, reports, submissions and \ndocumentation related to accreditation and QA processes; \n\uf06c To provide secretariat support to committees and working groups; \n\uf06c Supporting University functions as required (e.g. graduation ceremony, academic events, \nstudent recruitment exercise, etc.); and \n\uf06c To perform any other duties as assigned by the Head / Supervisor \n \n \nRequirements \n\uf06c Bachelor\u2019s degree holder; \n\uf06c Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; \n\uf06c Possess initiative in handling multiple tasks with tight timelines; \n\uf06c Be able to work independently while maintaining a high level of accuracy; \n\uf06c A team player with good interpersonal and communication skills; \n\uf06c For the position of Executive Officer, applicants should preferably possess four years or more \nof relevant post -qualification working experience  relating to programme development and \nquality assurance in the higher education sector. \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form and a curriculum vitae (CV) with the expected \nsalary to the Registrar at reg_recruit@hksyu.edu .   \n \nApplication Deadline: until the post is filled.  \n \nThe application form can be downloaded at  \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/download/Application%20Form%20for%20non-Academic%20Positions.doc \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/UAO/2026/Jun/uao_ao_marketing_ft_2026-06-30.pdf": {"title": "Admissions O\ufb03cer (Marke\ufffdng and Admissions)", "description": "Admissions O\ufb03cer (Marke\ufffdng and Admissions) \nHong Kong Shue Yan University, Registry   \nUniversity Admissions O\ufb03ce   \nWe are seeking a dynamic, digitally savvy, and highly organized professional to join our team. \nWhile this role sits within the Admissions O\ufb03ce, the primary focus is to drive the university\u2019s \ndigital transforma\ufffdon and brand presence. You will play a pivotal role in leading our website \nrevamp projects and execu\ufffdng comprehensive marke\ufffdng campaigns to engage prospec\ufffdve \nlocal, mainland, and overseas students. \nCore Responsibili\ufffdes: \n1. Lead Website Revamp Projects: Take full ownership of website revamps. Manage \nend-to-end project lifecycles with internal and external stakeholders, u\ufffdlizing strong \nexperience in UX/UI design, data migra\ufffdon, SEO, and web analy\ufffdcs (e.g., GA4). \n2. Drive Digital Marke\ufffdng Strategy: Develop and oversee a comprehensive digital \nmarke\ufffdng strategy. Create engaging content across key social media pla\ufffdorms, \norchestrate email newsleters, and launch targeted online campaigns to enhance \nprogramme visibility. \n3. End-to-End Campaign Management: Manage mul\ufffdmedia marke\ufffdng projects from \nconcept to comple\ufffdon, including video produc\ufffdon, online/o\ufb04ine adver\ufffdsing, and \ncon\ufffdnuous website management to e\ufb00ec\ufffdvely promote the university's o\ufb00erings. \n4. Event Coordina\ufffdon: Event-manage a diverse calendar of promo\ufffdonal ac\ufffdvi\ufffdes, \nincluding admissions seminars, Informa\ufffdon Day, school visits, and educa\ufffdon expos \nto atract quali\ufb01ed applicants. \n5. Admissions Support: Provide administra\ufffdve support to the core admissions team, \nincluding handling student enquiries and processing applica\ufffdons during peak cycles. \nKey Requirements: \n\u2022 A bachelor\u2019s degree in marke\ufffdng, communica\ufffdons, crea\ufffdve/web design or a related \n\ufb01eld at least 3 years\u2019 relevant experience. \n\u2022 Proven experience in web design project management and digital marke\ufffdng best \nprac\ufffdces is mandatory. Technical knowledge of web development is a strong plus. \n\u2022 Knowledge in digital graphic or video content crea\ufffdon using industry tools (e.g., \nAdobe Illustrator/Photoshop/Canva or Adobe Premiere/A\ufffder E\ufb00ects/CapCut) is \nhighly advantageous. \n\u2022 Fluency in English, Cantonese, and Mandarin, with excep\ufffdonal communica\ufffdon skills \nfor both professional wri\ufffdng and dynamic presenta\ufffdons. \n\u2022 Strong organiza\ufffdonal skills with the ability to manage mul\ufffdple projects \nsimultaneously in a fast-paced environment. \n \nApplica\ufffdon Methods:   \n1) Applicants should send a cover leter, an applica\ufffdon form and a curriculum vitae (CV) with \nexpected salary to the Director of University Admissions O\ufb03ce at newapp@hksyu.edu; \n2) Applica\ufffdon form can be downloaded \nat: htps://www.hksyu.edu/download/Applica\ufffdon%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Posi\ufffdons.doc  \nReview of applica\ufffdons will start as soon as possible and con\ufffdnue un\ufffdl the post is \ufb01lled.   \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/UAO/2026/Jun/uao_ao_media_ft_2026-06-30.pdf": {"title": "Admissions O\ufb03cer (Mul\ufffdmedia Produc\ufffdon)", "description": "Admissions O\ufb03cer (Mul\ufffdmedia Produc\ufffdon) \nHong Kong Shue Yan University, Registry   \nUniversity Admissions O\ufb03ce   \nWe are seeking a dynamic, crea\ufffdve, and highly skilled mul\ufffdmedia professional to join our \nteam. While this role o\ufb03cially sits within the Admissions O\ufb03ce, the primary focus is high-\nquality video edi\ufffdng and produc\ufffdon. You will play a pivotal role in crea\ufffdng engaging visual \nstorytelling aimed at promo\ufffdng our university and programmes to local, mainland, and \noverseas students. \nCore Responsibili\ufffdes: \n1. Mul\ufffdmedia Content Crea\ufffdon: Design and produce engaging mul\ufffdmedia and video \ncontent that aligns with current digital trends and marke\ufffdng insights. Tailor content \nspeci\ufb01cally for the university website, YouTube channel, and major social media \npla\ufffdorms (including Facebook, Instagram, WeChat, and Xiaohongshu). \n2. Post-Produc\ufffdon & Edi\ufffdng: Master the edi\ufffdng and post-produc\ufffdon work\ufb02ow to \nensure top-\ufffder visual quality, expertly incorpora\ufffdng music, sound design, color \ngrading, and visual e\ufb00ects (VFX) as needed. \n3. Video & Photo Shoo\ufffdng: Execute high-quality video produc\ufffdon from concept to \nwrap; hands-on experience in professional photography and photo shoo\ufffdng is a \nstrong plus. \n4. Team Collabora\ufffdon: Collaborate closely with internal academic and administra\ufffdve \nteams to ensure brand consistency, narra\ufffdve alignment, and \ufffdmely delivery of \ncontent. \n5. Event & Campaign Support: Support various admission events (e.g., Info Day, \neduca\ufffdon expos, school visits) and par\ufffdcipate in ad-hoc promo\ufffdonal projects to \nelevate the university's public pro\ufb01le. \nKey Requirements: \n\u2022 Higher diploma or degree in Film & Media, Crea\ufffdve Media, Adver\ufffdsing, Marke\ufffdng, \nor related \ufb01eld with a minimum of 2-3 years of relevant experience in video \nproduc\ufffdon. \n\u2022 Pro\ufb01cient in professional video edi\ufffdng and mo\ufffdon graphics using Adobe Premiere \nand A\ufffder E\ufb00ects. \n\u2022 Pro\ufb01cient with video produc\ufffdon equipment (cameras, ligh\ufffdng setups and audio gear \netc) across pre-produc\ufffdon, shoo\ufffdng and ligh\ufffdng.  \n\u2022 Familiarity with graphic design, sound produc\ufffdon, and/or 3D anima\ufffdon is an \nadvantage. \n\u2022 Submission of a por\ufffdolio or showreel is mandatory. Please include valid link(s) in \nyour cover leter or applica\ufffdon form.  \n\u2022 Fluent in writen and spoken English, Cantonese and Mandarin. \n \nApplica\ufffdon Methods:   \n1) Applicants should send a cover leter, an applica\ufffdon form and a curriculum vitae (CV) with \nexpected salary to the Director of University Admissions O\ufb03ce at newapp@hksyu.edu; \n2) Applica\ufffdon form can be downloaded \nat: htps://www.hksyu.edu/download/Applica\ufffdon%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Posi\ufffdons.doc  \nReview of applica\ufffdons will start as soon as possible and con\ufffdnue un\ufffdl the post is \ufb01lled.   \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CIEBPR/2026/Jul/ciebpr_pm_po_ft_2026-07-14.pdf": {"title": "Mrs. Dorothy Koo and Dr. Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice and", "description": "Mrs. Dorothy Koo and Dr. Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice and \nResearch of the Hong Kong Shue Yan University \n \nProject Manager/Project Officer  \n \nResponsibilities: \n\u2022 Develop and maintain project timelines and budgets. \n\u2022 Coordinate with stakeholders to ensure the successful development and delivery of the training \nprogram, and publicity events  \n\u2022 Manage the project website and other publicity channels. \n\u2022 Assist the project leaders to draft the progress, evaluation, and completion report \n\u2022 Any other responsibilities as assigned by the Centre Directors \n \nRequirements:  \n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree with a minimum of 3 years of project management experience for Project \nManager, and 1 years for Project Officer \n\u2022 Experience in managing large-scale education projects is preferred.  \n\u2022 Strong leadership, communication and problem-solving skills. \n\u2022 Proficiency in English and Chinese. \n\u2022 Familiarity with website and social media management preferred. \n \nApplication  \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter and \nan updated curriculum vitae to the Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary \nEvidence-based Practice & Research (ciebpr@hksyu.edu). Application form (research positions) can be \ndownloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/. All applications will be treated in strict confidence. \nOnly those who are shortlisted will be contacted. Closing Date: by July 31 or until position is filled. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CIEBPR/2026/Mar/ciepbr_po_eo_ft_2026-03-30.pdf": {"title": "Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice", "description": "Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice \nand Research \n \nHong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) \n \nProject Officer / Executive Officer \n \nThe Hong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) is seeking high-calibre candidates to join the Mrs \nDorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice and \nResearch.  The Centre hosts a community project that aspires to strengthen the social-emotional \ncapabilities of students and their parents, teachers, social workers, and the public.  The project \nincorporates gamification elements into social-emotional learning programmes for Primary 3 and 4 \nstudents. \n \nResponsibilities: \n\uf0b7 To provide administrative, clerical, financial, and operational support for the abovementioned \nproject; \n\uf0b7 To gather and maintain proper documentation and records; \n\uf0b7 To support evaluation and research studies; \n\uf0b7 To liaise with internal units, external suppliers and stakeholders; \n\uf0b7 To coordinate with the co-organizer and partner schools to facilitate the implementation of the \nproject; \n\uf0b7 To organize events, including public education activities and training sessions; \n\uf0b7 To assist in building the project brand, such as managing social media channels, conducting \npublicity campaigns, coordinating media interviews, drafting press releases, writing marketing \ncontent and implementing an SEO campaign; \n\uf0b7 To support for the enhancement of a gamified e-learning platform, a mobile application, \neducational materials, animation series and videos, etc.; \n\uf0b7 To supervise and provide guidance to student helpers; \n\uf0b7 To perform any other duties as assigned. \n \nRequirements: \n\uf0b7 A Bachelor\u2019s degree in Social Sciences, Marketing, Business Administration, or related \ndiscipline; \n\uf0b7 Preferably 2\u20133 years of relevant working experience; experience in the tertiary education sector \nwould be an advantage; \n\uf0b7 Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); \n\uf0b7 Proficiency in common office applications (e.g. MS Office Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook); \n\uf0b7 Ability to work both independently and collaboratively with efficiency and accuracy; \n\uf0b7 Strong organizational skill and attention to detail; \n\uf0b7 A strong sense of responsibility. \nCandidates with less experience and will be considered.  Fresh graduates are welcome to apply.  \n \nApplication: \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover \nletter and an updated curriculum vitae, to the Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for \nInterdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice & Research (ciebpr@hksyu.edu). \n \nApplication form (non-academic posts) can be downloaded \nat: https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ \n \nAll applications will be treated in strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be \ncontacted. \n \nClosing Date: 29 April 2026 or until the positions are filled, whichever is earlier. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/UAO/2026/Mar/uao_aa_ft_2026-03-03.pdf": {"title": "Admissions Assistant / Officer (Admissions Advisory", "description": "Admissions Assistant / Officer (Admissions Advisory \nand Administration)  \n \nHong Kong Shue Yan University, Registry  \nUniversity Admissions Office  \n \nWe are seeking a dynamic and organized Admissions Officer to join our team. You will play a \npivotal role in recruiting and supporting students from diverse backgrounds throughout the \nentire admissions journey. \n \nCore Responsibilities: \n1. Organize and manage a schedule of recruitment events locally and abroad, such as \nuniversity fairs, school visits, open days and admissions talks. \n2. Create and give presentations to prospective students and their parents and career \ncounsellors to promote the university's programmes and entry criteria. \n3. Advise prospective students on programme selection, admission requirements, \nscholarships, and the application steps. \n4. Oversee applications from start to finish, including reviewing applicant files and \nresponding to inquiries about application status. \n5. Manage the student visa process for non-local students, assisting with required \ndocuments and communicating with immigration officials. \n \nKey Requirements:  \n- A bachelor's degree. Applications from fresh graduates are welcome. \n- Excellent communication skills, with full professional proficiency and fluency \nin Cantonese and Mandarin and English. \n- Strong administrative and organizational skills, with keen attention to detail. \n- A customer-service oriented mindset, with the patience and empathy to guide prospective \nstudents. \n \nApplication Methods:  \n1)Applicants should send a cover letter and a curriculum vitae (CV) with expected salary to \nthe Director of University Admissions Office at newapp@hksyu.edu; or  \n 2)Complete the application form which can be downloaded at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Application%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Positions.doc, and send it together with a CV to newapp@hksyu.edu.  \n \nSalary and Conditions of Service  \nRemuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and \nexperience. Appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract and renewable with mutual \nconsent.  \n \nReview of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. \nApplicants with less experience may be considered for the post of Admissions Assistant.   \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely \nfor recruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment \nexercise. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/HMU/2026/Feb/hmu_ssossa_ft_2026-02-02.pdf": {"title": "Position: Student Services Officer / Student Services Assistant(Hall Management Unit)", "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \nPosition: Student Services Officer / Student Services Assistant(Hall Management Unit) \n \nThe appointee will be responsible for supporting Hall-based Student Engagement initiatives and providing a\ndministrative and logistical support to the Hall Management Unit. \n \nMajor Responsibilities \n\u25cf Assist in the development, coordination, and implementation of hall -based student engagement pro\ngrammes; \n\u25cf Support the coaching and supervision of student leaders in programme planning and hall-related ma\ntters; \n\u25cf Manage and update promotional channels, including programme websites; design promotional mate\nrials and maintain social media platforms; \n\u25cf Provide student support services, including front desk services, handling enquiries, managing check\n-in/check-out procedures, processing payments, and preparing monthly reports; \n\u25cf Provide operational and logistical support to Warden Teams as required; \n\u25cf Knowledge of video production and editing is an advantage; \n\u25cf Perform other duties as assigned. \n \nRequirements \n\u25cf Bachelor\u2019s degree or equivalent qualification; \n\u25cf Strong administrative abilities with excellent interpersonal skills; \n\u25cf Self-motivated, people-oriented, and with a strong sense of responsibility; \n\u25cf Demonstrated interest in and ability to handle student-related matters; \n\u25cf Good command of spoken and written English and Chinese, including Mandarin; \n\u25cf Prior working experience in student services or related fields will be an advantage. \n \nCandidates with more relevant experience may be considered for appointment as Student Services Officer. \n \nAppointment will be offered a two-years contract, with the possibility of renewal, subject to mutual agreem\nent. Application form can be obtained here. \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, resume and Cover Letter to Hall Management Unit, H\nong Kong Shue Yan University,10 Wai Tsui Crescent, Braemar Hill, North Point, H.K. or via email to tccha\nn@hksyu.edu. \n \nReview of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled.Only shortlisted app\nlicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for recruitment-related purpose. All a\npplications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/ESG/2026/Apr/esg_tomo_ft_2026-04-17.pdf": {"title": "Hong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) invites applications for the position of Technical", "description": "Hong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) invites applications for the position of Technical \nand Operations Manager / Officer under the Office of ESG and Sustainable \nDevelopment. The appointee will support campus development, building operation, and \nfacilities-related initiatives, with a focus on technical coordination, environmental \nperformance, and operational effectiveness across University campuses. \n \nMajor Responsibilities \n \nReporting to the Director, the appointee will be responsible for the technical and operational \naspects of campus facilities management, including but not limited to: \n \n\u2022 Supporting the planning, coordination, and implementation of ESG-related operational \ninitiatives, including energy efficiency measures, waste reduction programmes, and data \ncollection to support sustainability monitoring and institutional reporting \n\u2022 Supporting the planning, operation, and maintenance of University buildings and \nfacilities, including new campus developments and student hostel projects \n\u2022 Coordinating with the Facility Management Office on building services operation, \nmaintenance works, and facilities-related improvement initiatives \n\u2022 Conducting data collection and technical assessments related to carbon emissions, energy \nefficiency, and sustainability performance \n\u2022 Assisting in the preparation of technical reports, performance summaries, and institutional \nreports \n\u2022 Supporting the implementation of operational improvements related to building \nperformance, safety, operational effectiveness, and cost efficiency \n\u2022 Supporting procurement and contractor coordination related to facilities operation and \nmaintenance, with due consideration of sustainability criteria, life-cycle cost, and \nenvironmentally responsible practices \n\u2022 Liaising with internal units, consultants, and contractors on facilities management and \ncompliance-related matters, including environmental performance, sustainability \nrequirements, and relevant ESG-related standards \n\u2022 Performing other duties as assigned in support of campus operations and development \ninitiatives \nRequirements \nApplicants should possess: \n \n\u2022 A bachelor\u2019s degree or above in surveying, facilities management, building services \nengineering, mechanical or electrical engineering, environmental engineering, or a related \ndiscipline \n\u2022 At least three years of solid experience in facilities management, surveying, building \nservices operation, or technical operations, preferably in large-scale institutions, public \norganisations, or tertiary education settings \n\u2022 Professional qualification as a Registered Facility Manager (RFM) or Certified Facility \nManager (CFM) \n\u2022 Corporate or Professional Membership of the Hong Kong Institute of Facility Management \n(HKIFM) will be an advantage \n\u2022 Professional Membership of the Hong Kong Institute of Surveyors (MHKIS) will be an \nadvantage \n\u2022 Sound knowledge of building services systems, including electrical, mechanical, HVAC, \nfire services, and plumbing and drainage systems \n\u2022 Familiarity with ESG-related concepts, sustainability practices, and environmental \nperformance monitoring in facilities and campus operations \n\u2022 Understanding of relevant Hong Kong ordinances, regulations, and codes of practice related \nto building services operation, facilities management, and surveying practices \n\u2022 Experience in contractor coordination, technical documentation, surveying-related works, \nand operational monitoring \n\u2022 Strong organisational, analytical, and reporting skills \n\u2022 Ability to work independently and collaboratively with academic and administrative \nstakeholders \n\u2022 Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese \n \nAppointment and Benefits \nThe appointment will be made on a contract basis, with remuneration commensurate with \nqualifications and experience. Applicants should send a completed application form with \nexpected salary, together with a cover letter and an up-to-date curriculum vitae to Ms. \nBeatrice Wong (bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application form can be downloaded at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/. All applications will be treated in strict confidence. \nOnly those who are shortlisted will be contacted. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2025/Oct/rcdtbi_po_ft_2025-10-30.pdf": {"title": "Full Time Project Officers (Full-time)", "description": "Full Time Project Officers (Full-time) \nWe are hiring two Project Officers for the QESS project \u201cEnhancing Students\u2019 Emotional Wellness \nand Resilience in Post -secondary Institutions\u201d under the Research Center for Digital Education and \nBlended Intelligence, Hong Kong Shue Yan University. The project aims to enhance students\u2019 \nemotional wellness and resilience through an online platform, AI -powered consultation chatbot, and \nexperiential wellness programs. The Project Officers will support the planning, implementation, and \nevaluation of project activities, including coordinating workshops and events, managing \ndocumentation, designing surveys and promotional materials, analysing data, updating online \nplatforms, and liaising with Student Ambassadors, partner institutions, and technical vendors. \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities  \n\u2022 Plan, implement, and monitor project activities to ensure timely and effective execution. \n\u2022 Design and conduct evaluation studies, including data collection, analysis, and reporting. \n\u2022 Prepare comprehensive reports, engaging presentations, and concise evaluation summaries to \ncommunicate project findings and progress. \n\u2022 Coordinate and facilitate workshops, meetings, seminars, and training events to support project \ngoals. \n\u2022 Support and organise student activities and oversee the Student Ambassador Program, promoting \nmental wellness and resilience. \n\u2022 Develop and design promotional materials, including posters, infographics, and content for social \nmedia platforms. \n\u2022 Update and maintain the project website and online learning platform to ensure accurate and \ncurrent information. \n\u2022 Liaise with partner institutions, external collaborators, Student Ambassadors, and technical \nvendors to foster strong relationships and ensure seamless communication. \n\u2022 Maintain project documentation, including budgets, progress reports, and other records, ensuring \ncompliance with organisational standards. \nQualifications and Requirements  \n\u2022 A Bachelor\u2019s degree or above in Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, IT Management, or \nrelated disciplines. \n\u2022 Experience in data collection/analysis, survey design, and/or project coordination preferred. \n\u2022 Proficiency in design tools (e.g., Adobe Illustrator) and data analysis software (SPSS, Mplus, R) \nis an advantage. \n\u2022 Strong organizational, writing, and interpersonal skills. \n\u2022 Proficiency in English and Chinese. \n\u2022 Interest in promoting student mental health and wellness. \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up- to-date curriculum vitae to Ms.  Beatrice Wong ( bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application \nform can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ . All applications will be treated \nin strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted.  \nClosing Date: by 20 November 2025 or until the position is filled.   "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2025/Oct/rcdtbi_po_pm_ft_2025-10-30.pdf": {"title": "AI-Enhanced Teaching Resource Hub for the Self -Financing Higher Education Sector\u201d  under", "description": "Full Time Project Officer / Project Manager  \nWe are hiring one Project Officer and one Project Manager  for the QESS project \u201cDeveloping an \nAI-Enhanced Teaching Resource Hub for the Self -Financing Higher Education Sector\u201d  under \nthe Research Center for Digital Education and Blended Intelligence, Hong Kong Shue Yan University. \nThis inter-institutional project aims to identify, centralize, and utilize AI learning resources and tools \nto support teaching and the development of A I literacy among post -secondary teachers, provide \neffective AI tools for teaching in self -financing institutions, organize professional development \nactivities, and conduct research to evaluate AI literacy initiatives. \nThe Project Officer / Project Manager will lead and coordinate all aspects of the project, ensuring \ntimely completion of deliverables, smooth collaboration among teams, and effective implementation \nof the AI-Enhanced Teaching Resource Hub. \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities \n\u2022 Plan, implement, and monitor project activities, ensuring milestones are achieved on time and \nwithin budget. \n\u2022 Oversee the development and maintenance of the online AI-Enhanced Teaching Resource Hub, \nincluding functionality, accessibility, and scalability. \n\u2022 Coordinate with technical teams, faculty contributors, and subject matter experts to integrate AI \ntools, preloaded prompts, lesson planning tools, and assessment features. \n\u2022 Manage content creation and organization for the platform, including training session videos, \nteaching showcases, and self-learning materials. \n\u2022 Organize and support professional development activities such as workshops, Coffee Talk \nmeetings, and public seminars; handle registrations, promotions, and resource distribution. \n\u2022 Track platform analytics, participation data, and engagement metrics; prepare progress reports \nand final reports for stakeholders and funding bodies. \n\u2022 Liaise with partner institutions, external collaborators, technical vendors and project teams to \nensure smooth collaboration and communication. \n\u2022 Manage project documentation, budget tracking, procurement, and other administrative tasks. \nQualifications and Requirements \n\u2022 A Bachelor\u2019s degree or above in Education, Information Technology, Psychology, Social \nSciences, or a related discipline. \n\u2022 At least 2-3 years\u2019 experience in project management in educational or research settings. \n\u2022 Experience in liaising with technical vendors or digital project teams is an advantage. \n\u2022 Strong organizational, communication, writing, and interpersonal skills. \n\u2022 Proficiency in English and Chinese. \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up- to-date curriculum vitae to Ms . Beatrice Wong ( bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application \nform can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ . All applications will be treated \nin strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted.  \nClosing Date: by 20 November 2025 or until the position is filled.   "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CSC/2026/Oct/csc_it_pt_2026-10-06.pdf": {"title": "Position: Part-time Audio Visual (AV) Technician", "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \nComputing Services Centre \n \nPosition: Part-time Audio Visual (AV) Technician \nMajor Responsibilities: \n\u2022 Provide frontline Audio Visual (AV) and IT support for  staff and students under the \nUser Services Section, ensuring smooth daily operations within the Computing \nServices Centre and across the University. \n\u2022 Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues for both IT hardware/software and Audio \nVisual (AV) systems. \n\u2022 Set up, operate, and maintain AV equipment in classrooms, conference rooms, and \nsupport event venues. \n\u2022 Provide flexible, on-demand IT support (remote, phone or on- site) for urgent or non -\noffice hours situations). \n\u2022 Work independently and manage assigned responsibilities effectively. \n\u2022 Perform ad-hoc tasks, special assignments, and other tasks as assigned. \n \nRequirements: \n\u2022 Diploma or above in Multimedia Technology, I T, Computer Science, or a related \ndiscipline from a recognized University, College, or Technical Institute. \n\u2022 Minimum of 2 years of relevant experience in AV support, IT support, or a related field. \n\u2022 Hands-on experience with Zoom, Teams, and control systems. \n\u2022 Good knowledge of PC hardware, software, and troubleshooting techniques. \n\u2022 Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. \n\u2022 Good interpersonal, communication, and customer service skills. \n\u2022 Good command of both spoken and written English and Chinese  (Cantonese and \nMandarin). \n \nKey Details: \n\u2022 Employment Type: Part-time \n\u2022 Working Hours: Evening shifts on scheduled teaching days, typically from 6:00pm \u2013 \n9:00pm, five days per week. \n\u2022 Start Date: Immediate availability is highly preferred / As soon as available \n\u2022 Remuneration: Salary will be commensurate with qualification and experience. \n \nApplicants should apply by sending a completed application form, resume and Cover Letter via \nemail to cscjob@hksyu.edu. \n \nDeadline: The posts are open until filled. \nPlease complete the application form via the hyperlink below: \nhttps://eform2.hksyu.edu/view.php?id=15970 \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used for recruitment \npurposes only. Applications will receive full consideration until the positions are filled.  "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2025/Oct/rcdtbi_AI_programmer_ft_2025-10-30.pdf": {"title": "We are hiring an  AI Programmer  for the QESS project \u201cDeveloping an AI -Enhanced Teaching", "description": "Full-time AI Programmer  \nWe are hiring an  AI Programmer  for the QESS project \u201cDeveloping an AI -Enhanced Teaching \nResource Hub for the Self-Financing Higher Education Sector\u201d under the Research Center for Digital \nEducation and Blended Intelligence, Hong Kong Shue Yan University. This inter-institutional project \naims to centralize and utilize AI learning resources and tools to support teaching and the development \nof AI literacy among post-secondary teachers across four self-financing higher education institutions, \nprovide effective AI tools for teaching in self -financing institutions, organize professional \ndevelopment activities, and conduct research to evaluate AI literacy initiatives. \nThe AI Programmer will develop, integrate, and maintain educational AI tools and features for the AI-\nEnhanced Teaching Resource Hub, working closely with faculty, internal tech teams, and other project \nstaff. \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities \n\u2022 Develop and integrate advanced AI features into the Teaching Resource Hub. \n\u2022 Customize educational AI tools for specific subject content and teaching needs. \n\u2022 Ensure the platform\u2019s functionality, scalability, security, and smooth integration of AI tools. \n\u2022 Troubleshoot technical issues and implement updates based on user feedback and analytics. \n\u2022 Conduct testing and quality assurance for all AI tools and platform features. \n\u2022 Collaborate with technical vendors and the internal tech team to support platform and AI tool \ndevelopment. \n\u2022 Support the development and implementation of ethical guidelines for AI usage within the \nplatform. \nQualifications and Requirements \n\u2022 A Bachelor\u2019s degree or above in Computer Science, Information Technology, Data Science, or a \nrelated field. \n\u2022 Experience in AI development, programming, or educational technology preferred. \n\u2022 Proficiency in programming languages and AI frameworks relevant to platform development. \n\u2022 Strong problem-solving, analytical, and communication skills. \n\u2022 Proficiency in English and Chinese. \n\u2022 Interest in applying AI to enhance teaching and learning in higher education. \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up- to-date curriculum vitae to Ms . Beatrice Wong ( bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application \nform can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ . All applications will be treated \nin strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted.  \nClosing Date: by 20 November 2025 or until the position is filled.   \n \n  \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CHI/2026/Oct/chi_ra_pt_2026-10-06.pdf": {"title": "\u5927\u5b78\u7814\u8cc7\u6703\u7814\u7a76\u8a08\u5283\uff08\u7de8\u865f UGC/FDS15/H12/21\uff09\u64ec\u62db\u8058\u517c\u8077\u7814\u7a76\u52a9\u7406\u5169\u540d\uff0c\u9700", "description": "\u5927\u5b78\u7814\u8cc7\u6703\u7814\u7a76\u8a08\u5283\uff08\u7de8\u865f UGC/FDS15/H12/21\uff09\u64ec\u62db\u8058\u517c\u8077\u7814\u7a76\u52a9\u7406\u5169\u540d\uff0c\u9700\n\u65bc 2026 \u5e74 11 \u6708\u5230\u8077\uff0c\u8a08\u5283\u8cc7\u6599\u5982\u4e0b\uff1a  \n \nProject Reference No.: UGC/FDS15/H07/25 \nName and Institution of the Principal Investigator: \nDr. WONG Ka Ki (Hong Kong Shue Yan University) \nTitle of Project: \nTranslation of Third World literature in Communist Periodicals in the Cold War \nHong Kong (1948-1969) \n\u51b7\u6230\u6642\u671f\u9999\u6e2f\u89aa\u5171\u5831\u520a\u7684\u7b2c\u4e09\u4e16\u754c\u6587\u5b78\u7ffb\u8b6f\uff081948-1969\uff09 \n \n\u517c\u8077\u7814\u7a76\u52a9\u7406\u8077\u8cac\u5982\u4e0b\uff1a \n1\u3001\u53d7\u8058\u671f\u5927\u7d04 8 \u500b\u6708\uff08\u5982\u53d7\u50f1\u671f\u9593\u672a\u80fd\u5b8c\u6210\u5de5\u4f5c\u5167\u5bb9\uff0c\u9808\u8996\u4e4e\u8cc7\u52a9\u60c5\u6cc1\u6c7a\u5b9a\u80fd\n\u5426\u5ef6\u9577\u50f1\u7528\u671f\uff09\uff1b \n2\u3001\u641c\u96c6\u7814\u7a76\u8cc7\u6599\uff0c\u4e3b\u8981\u662f\u5fae\u7e2e\u81a0\u5377\u5831\u520a\u6750\u6599\uff0c\u4e5f\u53ef\u80fd\u5305\u62ec\u7db2\u4e0a\u8cc7\u6599\u5eab\u3001\u5be6\u9ad4\u66f8\n\u7c4d\u5831\u520a\u7b49\uff1b \n3\u3001\u6574\u7406\u6a94\u6848\u3001\u8f38\u5165\u53ca\u6821\u5c0d\u8cc7\u6599\uff1b \n4\u3001\u5176\u4ed6\u8207\u672c\u7814\u7a76\u8a08\u5283\u76f8\u95dc\u7684\u6587\u66f8\u5de5\u4f5c\u3002 \n \n\u517c\u8077\u7814\u7a76\u52a9\u7406\u61c9\u5fb5\u689d\u4ef6\u5982\u4e0b\uff1a \n \n1\u3001\u5177\u4e2d\u570b\u8a9e\u8a00\u6587\u5b78\u6216\u76f8\u95dc\u5b78\u7cfb\u7684\u78a9\u58eb\u6216\u4ee5\u4e0a\u5b78\u4f4d\uff1b \n2\u3001\u5c08\u7814\u9999\u6e2f\u6587\u5b78\u8005\u512a\u5148\u8003\u616e\uff1b \n3\u3001\u9808\u719f\u6089\u641c\u96c6\u53ca\u6574\u7406\u5831\u520a\u6750\u6599\uff1b \n4\u3001\u5de5\u4f5c\u52e4\u61c7\u3001\u5177\u8cac\u4efb\u611f\u3001\u8655\u4e8b\u8b39\u614e\u7d30\u5fc3\u3002 \n\u85aa\u916c\u9762\u8b70\u3002 \n\u9644\u8a3b\uff1a  \n1. \u8acb\u4e0b\u8f09\u4e26\u586b\u5beb\u7533\u8acb\u8868\uff0c\u53e6\u9644\u500b\u4eba\u7c21\u6b77\u548c\u7e73\u4ea4\u76f8\u95dc\u6587\u4ef6\u8cc7\u6599\uff1b  \n2. \u8acb\u9644\u4e0a\u8fd1\u671f\u5f69\u8272\u8b49\u4ef6\u7167\u4e00\u5f35\uff1b  \n3. \u8acb\u9644\u4e0a\u5b78\u4f4d\u8b49\u66f8\uff0c\u53ca\u8077\u696d\u8cc7\u683c\u8b49\u66f8\u3001\u7372\u734e\u8b49\u66f8\u4e4b\u985e\u8b49\u660e\u6587\u4ef6\uff08\u82e5\u9069\u5408\uff09\u7684\u6383\u63cf\n\u7248\u6216\u5f71\u5370\u672c\u3002 \n \n\u96fb\u90f5\u81f3\uff1akkwong@hksyu.edu \u738b\u5bb6\u742a\u535a\u58eb\uff08\u90f5\u4ef6\u4e3b\u984c\uff1a\u61c9\u5fb5\u517c\u8077\u7814\u7a76\u52a9\u7406\uff09  \n\u6216\u90f5\u5bc4\u81f3\uff1a\u9999\u6e2f\u6a39\u4ec1\u5927\u5b78\u4e2d\u570b\u8a9e\u8a00\u6587\u5b78\u7cfb \u738b\u5bb6\u742a\u535a\u58eb\uff08\u4fe1\u5c01\u4e0a\u8acb\u8a3b\u660e\uff1a\u61c9\u5fb5\u517c\n\u8077\u7814\u7a76\u52a9\u7406\uff09  \n\u62db\u8058\u671f \uff1a \u5373\u65e5\u8d77\u81f32026 \u5e74 10 \u6708 30 \u65e5 \u6b62\u3002 \uff08\u9074\u9078\u7a0b\u5e8f\u65bc\u6536\u5230\u7533\u8acb\u6750\u6599\u5373\u6642\u958b\u59cb\uff09 \n \n\u7533\u8acb\u8005\u5c07\u65bc\u905e\u4ea4\u5168\u90e8\u6240\u9700\u6750\u6599\u56db\u9031\u5167\u7372\u9080\u9762\u8a66\u3002\u60df\u5165\u9078\u9762\u8a66\u8005\u65b9\u7372\u767c\u901a\u77e5 \u3002\u6240\u6709\n\u7533\u8acb\u8cc7\u6599\u53ea\u4f5c\u62db\u8058\u4e4b\u7528\u3002 "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SW/2026/May/sw_ra_pt_2026-05-28.pdf": {"title": "Department of Social Work: Part-time Research Assistant (One Position for 12 months)", "description": "Department of Social Work: Part-time Research Assistant (One Position for 12 months)  \nJob duties:  \nThe RA will assist the Principal Investigator (PI) to conduct research project entitled \u201cExploring the role \nof social capital in community-based sharing: The case of community living room (URG/25/08)\u201d, which is \nfunded by the Hong Kong Shue Yan University\u2019s University Research Fund. The appointee will be \nresponsible for the following tasks:  \na. Assisting with literature review \nb. Liaising with research collaborators and partners \nc. Conducting interviews \nd. Draft research report \ne. Other assigned duties \n \nRequirements:  \nApplicants should have: A bachelor degree in social sciences or a related discipline (preferred). \nKnolwedge in qualitative research methods. Proficiency in computer software applications. Ability to \nwork independently and collaboratively. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English and \nChinese. The appointment will be made on the basis of a one-year contract, with a possibility of \nrenewal, subject to mutual agreement and funding availability. The remuneration package will be \ncommensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication:  \nApplicants should submit a completed application form along with a CV to Dr. Lai Ka Wai (Principal \nInvestigator) at mkwlai@hksyu.edu. \n \nApplication Forms (academic positions) can be obtained at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy. All application materials will be treated in strict \nconfidence. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CIEBPR/2026/May/ciebpr_cpsy_ft_2026-05-08.pdf": {"title": "Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice", "description": "Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice \nand Research \n \nHong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) \n \nCounselling Psychologist \n \nThe Hong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) is seeking high-calibre candidates to join the Mrs \nDorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice and \nResearch. The Centre hosts a community project that aspires to strengthen the social-emotional \ncapabilities of students and their parents, teachers, social workers, and the public.  The project \nincorporates gamification elements into social-emotional learning programmes for Primary 3 and 4 \nstudents. \n \nResponsibilities: \n\u2022 Design integrative and gamified emotional learning materials tailored social emotional learning \n\u2022 Provide consultation services to students, parents, and teachers participating in the project \n\u2022 Deliver outreach psycho-educational/ consultation service to schools \n\u2022 Assist in conducting research-related tasks, including data collection, analysis and report \nwriting etc. \n\u2022 Assist in the development and execution of publicity events related \n\u2022 Assist in drafting progress reports and evaluation studies as required by project manager \n\u2022 Any other responsibilities as assigned by the Centre Directors  \n \nRequirements: \n\u2022 Master\u2019s degree in Counselling Psychology and Registered Counselling Psychologist of the \n\u201cHong Kong Psychological Society\u201d preferred \n\u2022 Three years or above of counselling experience in an educational or related setting \n\u2022 Proficiency in SPSS, along with experience in both quantitative and qualitative data collection \nand analysis \n\u2022 Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively in a team environment \n\u2022 Proficiency in spoken and written English and Chinese \n \nApplication: \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover \nletter and an updated curriculum vitae, to the Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for \nInterdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice & Research (ciebpr@hksyu.edu). \n \nApplication form (research positions) can be downloaded \nat: https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ \n \nAll applications will be treated in strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be \ncontacted. \n \nClosing Date: 25 May or until the positions are filled, whichever is earlier. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/EF/2026/Jan/ef_ra_ft_pt_2026-01-19.pdf": {"title": "project team now seeks to appoint a passionate candidate for the position of Research", "description": "Supported by the Faculty Development Scheme (FDS) 2025/26 Exercise, Research Grants \nCouncil with reference no. UGC/FDS15/B01/25, a project team from the Department of \nEconomics and Finance, Hong Kong Shue Yan University will conduct a two-year research \nproject entitled \u201cExamining Impacts of Channel Addition/Elimination on Perceived Control \nand Concern about Cybersecurity: A Scenario-based Survey Study of Virtual Banking\u201d. The \nproject team now seeks to appoint a passionate candidate for the position of Research \nAssistant (Full-time / Part-time) for the project. \n \nResearch Assistant (Full-time / Part-time) \nThe major responsibilities of the appointee will be: \n\u2022 Conduct literature review, data collection and data analysis \n\u2022 Assist in the compilation of research reports and other forms of deliverables \n\u2022 Perform other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team \n \nRequirements \nApplicants should possess: \n\u2022 Preferably a bachelor\u2019s degree with some quantitative research experience \n\u2022 Good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese \n\u2022 Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently and meet tight deadlines \n \nThe Appointment commences on 1st Jan 2026 to 31st December 2026. The remuneration \npackage will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae to the Principal Investigator of the project Dr LEE Tin Yun Philip \n[tylee@hksyu.edu]. Application form can be obtained at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy  \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely \nfor recruitment-related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment \nexercise. \n \nDeadline \nUntil the position is filled. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/Oct/counpsy_ra_ft_2026-10-09.pdf": {"title": "Job Title: Research Assistant [2 positions]", "description": "Job Title: Research Assistant [2 positions] \nMode: Full-time \nAppointment Period: 4-6 months with the possibility of renewal subject to mutual agreement \nDepartment: Department of Counselling & Psychology (Brain Stimulation Laboratory) \nClosing Date: October 31st 2026 \n \n(1) Project Assistant  \nJob Duties \nThe appointee will be responsible for (a) conducting quantitative and qualitative research studies, \nincluding research design, data collection, analysis, compilation of reports and other \nforms of deliverables; (b) providing administrative support to the director (Dr. Bess Lam); (c) \nPreparing literature review regarding neuroscience and psychology; (d) compiling progress reports \nand the final report; e) assisting the publications and other related research work in the laboratory; and \nf) maintaining laboratory equipment and ensure compliance with safety protocols. Supportive \nsupervision will be provided upon appointment. \n \nRequirements \nApplicants should have \n(a) bachelor\u2019s degree in Psychology or a related field; \n(b) excellent command of SPSS; \n(c) good skills in psychology- related data collection; \n(d) excellent command of English and Chinese language (Cantonese); \n(e) personal quality of good responsibility, industriousness and readiness to learn and to help other \npeople. \n \n \nFunding information \nThese posts are funded by Research Grant Matching Scheme (RMGS) and the private donation from \nImpactHK for the homeless and children mental health projects. Salary will be commensurate with \nqualifications and experience.  \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter, and a curriculum \nvitae (CV) to: Dr. Bess Lam at Email yhlam@hksyu.edu with the subject \u201capplication for \nproject assistant\u201d. It would be nice if the applicant could also attach to the email a sample of his or her \nuniversity assignments or research papers that can demonstrate his or her proficiency in English \nwriting. Application forms can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/tc/about/career/ \nAll applicants will be treated in strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/Mar/counpsy_ra_2026-03-05.pdf": {"title": "Research Assistant (Full Time/ Part Time)", "description": "Research Assistant (Full Time/ Part Time) \nDepartment of Counselling and Psychology \nThe appointee will work on a project named \u201cProvision of Services for Basic, Advanced and/or Thematic \nCourses for Teacher Professional Development on Catering for Students with Special Educational Needs \nfor the 2024/25, 2025/26 and 2026/27 School Years\u201d. \nResponsibilities \n\u2022 Assisting in implementing research projects under the supervision of the Program coordinator \nand Project Manager, including literature review, data collection, entry, processing and analysis, \ndraft report and other research duties assigned. \n\u2022 Providing programme and secretariat support \n\u2022 Liaising with internal and external parties \n\u2022 Organizing events/functions/visits \n\u2022 System work and office management \n\u2022 Performing any other duties as assigned \nRequirements \n\u2022 Bachelor's degree \n\u2022 Preferably with several years of post-qualification working experience \n\u2022 Have good interpersonal and communication skills \n\u2022 Proficiency in both spoken and written English and Chinese \n\u2022 Literary in computer applications \n\u2022 Self-motivated and able to work independently or as a team member \nImmediate availability is preferred. \nFor enquiries, please contact Ms. Twinkle Lam via e-mail: sclam@hksyu.edu \n \nApplication Procedure \nApplicants should send a letter of application together with curriculum vitae to the following address or \nby email: \nMs. Twinkle Lam \nDepartment of Counselling & Psychology \nHong Kong Shue Yan University, \n10 Wai Tsui Crescent, \nBraemar Hill, Hong Kong \nE-mail: sclam@hksyu.edu \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data collected will be used for staff recruitment \npurposes only. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/Mar/counpsy_ra_pt_2026-03-02.pdf": {"title": "Position: Part-time Research Assistant", "description": "Position: Part-time Research Assistant \nJob Duties \nThe part-time RA will assist the Principal Investigator (PI) to conduct research project \nentitled  \u201c Efficacy of a mindfulness -based intervention with and without virtual reality \nsupport to promote mental health through self-compassion and mind wandering among \nuniversity students: A randomised controlled trial  (URG/24/07)\u201d , which is funded by the \nHong Kong Shue Yan University\u2019s University Research Fund. \n \nMajor Responsibilities  \n\u2022 Collecting, entering, processing, and analysing data \n\u2022 Liaising with different parties for data collection \n\u2022 Assist in group sessions \n\u2022 Perform other research and administrative duties as assigned by the PI to support \nthe operation of the research project \n \nRequirements  \nApplicants should possess:  \n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree in counselling, psychology, social work, or related disciplines \n\u2022 Preferably with both qualitative and quantitative research experience \n\u2022 Preferably with experience in mindfulness and/or facilitating group sessions \n\u2022 Strong command of written and spoken English and Chinese \n\u2022 Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently, and capable of meeting tight \ndeadlines \n\u2022 Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills \n\u2022 Proficient computer skills, including MS Office applications and SPSS \n \nThe Appointment commences as soon as possible  to 30 June 2026. The remuneration \npackage will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  \n \nApplication  \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae with the expected salary to Dr. Winnie Yuen (the PI)  at \nwyyuen@hksyu.edu.  Application form can be obtained at:  \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used \nsolely for recruitment -related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the \nrecruitment exercise.  \n \nClosing Date \nUntil the position is filled. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2025/Dec/counpsy_ra_ft_2025-12-23.pdf": {"title": "Research Assistant (Full-time, 4-month Fixed Contract)", "description": " \n \nResearch Assistant (Full-time, 4-month Fixed Contract) \nProject Title: \nVirtual Reality\u2013Based Cognitive Behavioral Therapy for Social Anxiety\u2013Driven \nDepression among Youths: A Randomized Controlled Trial (UGC/FDS15/H14/24) \u57fa\n\u65bc\u865b\u64ec\u73fe\u5be6\u7684\u8a8d\u77e5\u884c\u70ba\u6cbb\u7642\u5c0d\u793e\u4ea4\u7126\u616e\u578b\u6291\u9b31\u9752\u5c11\u5e74\u7684\u6548\u679c\u7814\u7a76\uff1a\u4e00\u9805\u96a8\u6a5f\u5c0d\n\u7167\u5be6\u9a57 \n \nJob Responsibilities \n\u2022 Support the implementation of a VR-based psychological intervention for \nyouths with social anxiety and depression. \n\u2022 Work closely with the project team and liaise with different stakeholders, \nincluding schools, NGOs, and research staff. \n\u2022 Assist with participant recruitment, intervention delivery, data collection, and \nfollow-up arrangements. \n\u2022 Carry out other research and administrative tasks as assigned by the team \nleader. \nRequirements \n\u2022 Registered counseling psychologist or holder of a related professional \nqualification. \n\u2022 Familiar with Cognitive Behavioral Therapy. \n\u2022 Able to work independently and take initiative. \n\u2022 Self-motivated, responsible, and able to work well in a team. \n\u2022 Strong interpersonal and communication skills. \n\u2022 Able to fully commit to the project from Monday to Friday; occasional work \noutside regular working hours may be required, depending on project needs. \n\u2022 Fluent in Chinese and English (Cantonese, Mandarin, and English). \nThis role is quite intensive, but it offers an excellent opportunity to quickly \naccumulate around 300 hours of direct counseling practice. Applicants should \nhave strong time management skills, be able to work well under pressure, and \ndemonstrate a high degree of flexibility. \nPreferred Qualifications \n \n \n\u2022 Experience working with children or adolescents. \n\u2022 Interest in or familiarity with technology-assisted interventions, such as VR. \n\u2022 Able to start work as soon as possible. \nWhat You Will Gain \n\u2022 Substantial clinical exposure through direct involvement in intervention \ndelivery. \n\u2022 Hands-on experience in research implementation, data collection, and \nteamwork. \n\u2022 Strong preparation for future research postgraduate applications or advanced \nclinical training. \nAppointment Details \n\u2022 Contract period: 4 months (initially), with the possibility of extension \ndepending on project progress and mutual agreement \n\u2022 Salary: HKD 21,000 per month (fixed) \n\u2022 Closing date: Until the position is filled \nApplication Method \nInterested applicants should send: \n1. A completed application form (including job expectation) \n2. An updated CV \nto Dr. WANG Yi-Zhou Joe by email: ywang@hksyu.edu "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SOC/2026/Mar/soc_ra_pt_2026-03-23.pdf": {"title": "Part -time Research Assistant in EEG -Driven VR Systems for Emotional Regulation", "description": "Part -time Research Assistant in EEG -Driven VR Systems for Emotional Regulation \nResearch  (Ref: URG/ 25/06) \nPosition: Part-time Research Assistant (Start date: May 2026) \nProject Details:  MindScapes: EEG-Driven Virtual Reality for Emotional Regulation and \nUser-Centric Testing \nThis research project investigates the integration of real-time EEG biofeedback with \nimmersive VR environments to support emotional regulation and mental well-being. \nThe study focuses on developing and validating an accessible, user-centered system \nthat combines art therapy principles, meditation techniques, and culturally-inspired \nspatial design. Through structured user testing, the project aims to refine the system's \nadaptive feedback mechanisms and evaluate its effectiveness in promoting emotional \nrelief and self-awareness. (PI: Miss Xinzhou ZHANG) \n \nKey Responsibilities:  \nThe appointee will assist the Principal Investigator in the following tasks: \n\u2022 Organizing and coordinating user testing sessions, including participant scheduling \nand venue setup \n\u2022 Recording and documenting user interactions during VR testing sessions \n\u2022 Collecting and organizing quantitative data (EEG metrics, engagement duration, \nsystem performance) \n\u2022 Assisting with the administration and collection of questionnaires and feedback forms \n\u2022 Transcribing and organizing qualitative data from semi-structured interviews \n\u2022 Maintaining organized databases of user testing results and feedback \n\u2022 Supporting prototype iteration and debugging processes when needed \n\u2022 Assisting with preliminary data analysis and visualization \n\u2022 Contributing to the preparation of research documentation and reports \n \nRequirements:  \n\u2022 A bachelor's degree or current enrollment in a program related to Psychology, \nSociology, Human-Computer Interaction, Digital Media, Computer Science, or related \ndisciplines \n\u2022 Strong organizational skills and attention to detail in data collection and management \n\u2022 Basic familiarity with VR technology and user experience testing (training will be \nprovided) \n\u2022 Excellent interpersonal skills for participant interaction and coordination \n\u2022 Proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese/Putonghua) \n\u2022 Experience with data entry and basic statistical software (e.g., Excel, SPSS) is an \nadvantage \n\u2022 Interest in mental health, meditation, or emotional well-being research is preferred \n\u2022 Ability to work independently and maintain confidentiality of research data \n \nTerms of Appointment:  \n\u2022 The appointment is on a part-time basis (approximately 10-15 hours per week during \ntesting phases, totaling 70 hours over the project period) \n\u2022 Working hours will be flexible but may include some weekends to accommodate \nparticipant availability \n\u2022 Remuneration: HK$100 per hour \n\u2022 Duration: June 2026 - September 2026 (approximately 3 months) \n \nApplication Procedure:  \nInterested candidates should send a cover letter and CV to Miss Xinzhou ZHANG via \nemail at [xzzhang@hksyu.edu] by April 30. \nReview of applications will commence immediately and continue until the position is \nfilled. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for an interview. \nThe University reserves the right not to fill this position or to fill the position by invitation. \nPersonal data provided by applicants will be used for recruitment purposes only. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/EF/2025/Nov/ef_ra_pt_ft_2025-11-04.pdf": {"title": "Research Assistant (Full-time / Part-time)", "description": "Supported by the Faculty Development Scheme (FDS) 2025/26 Exercise, Research Grants Council \nwith reference no. UGC/FDS15/E04/25, a project team from the Department of Economics and \nFinance, Hong Kong Shue Yan University will conduct a two-year research project entitled \u201cA Green \nStructural Efficiency Framework for New Quality Productive Forces\u201d . The project team now seeks \nto appoint a high-calibre candidate for the position of Research Assistant (Full-time / Part-time) for \nthe project.  \nResearch Assistant (Full-time / Part-time) \nThe major responsibilities of the appointee will be:  \n\u2022 Conduct literature review, data collection and data analysis \n\u2022 Assist in the compilation of research reports and other forms of deliverables \n\u2022 Perform other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team \nRequirements  \nApplicants should possess:  \n\u2022 A bachelor\u2019s degree, preferably with some quantitative research experience \n\u2022 Good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese \n\u2022 Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently and meet tight deadlines \nThe Appointment commences on 1st Jan 2026 to 31st December 2027. The remuneration package \nwill be commensurate with quali\ufb01cations and experience.  \nApplication  \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a curriculum \nvitae to the Principal Investigator of the project Dr TSANG Chun-kei [cktsang@hksyu.edu]. \nApplication form can be obtained at: https://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy  \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise.  \nDeadline  \nUntil the position is \ufb01lled. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2026/Jul/rcdebi_ra_ft_2026-07-15.pdf": {"title": "Full-Time Research Assistant", "description": "Full-Time Research Assistant \nWe are hiring a Research Assistant   under the Research Center for Digital Education and Blended \nIntelligence, Hong Kong Shue Yan University. The Research Assistant will support research related \nto digital pedagogy and well-being.  \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities \n\u2022 Conduct literature reviews and synthesize research on digital pedagogy, blended intelligence, and \nwell-being. \n\u2022 Assist in designing research instruments and coordinating data collection activities (surveys, \ninterviews, and focus groups). \n\u2022 Perform quantitative and qualitative data analysis and manage project databases. \n\u2022 Support the implementation, testing, and user-support of digital learning platforms and well-\nbeing tools. \n\u2022 Assist in drafting research ethics applications, progress reports, grant proposals, and academic \nmanuscripts. \n\u2022 Coordinate communication between the Research Center, investigators, school partners, and \nstakeholders. \n\u2022 Assist in organizing academic seminars, workshops, and knowledge transfer events. \n\u2022 Handle day-to-day project administration, including tracking timelines, maintaining records, and \nscheduling meetings. \nQualifications and Requirements \n\u2022 A Bachelor\u2019s degree or above in Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, or a related discipline. \n\u2022 Experience in research, data collection, and analysis preferred. \n\u2022 Proficiency in data analysis software (SPSS, Mplus, R) is an advantage. \n\u2022 Strong organizational, writing, analytical, and interpersonal skills. \n\u2022 Proficiency in English and Chinese. \n\u2022 Interest in educational research and supporting teaching innovation through AI. \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up-to-date curriculum vitae to Dr Jason CHOW (tschow@hksyu.edu) . The Application form \ncan be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/. All applications will be treated in strict \nconfidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted.  \nClosing Date: by 10 August 2026 or until the position is filled.   \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2026/Feb/rcdtbi_ra_ft_2026-02-12.pdf": {"title": "Full-Time Research Assistant", "description": "Full-Time Research Assistant \nWe are hiring a Research Assistant under the Research Center for Digital Education and Blended \nIntelligence, Hong Kong Shue Y an University. This position supports projects that identify, centralize, \nand utilize digital technologies and tools to enhance mental health support and learning outcomes. The \nrole involves conducting research to evaluate digital teaching and mental health programs, designing \neffective digital tools for mental health and learning, and organizing professional development \nactivities.  \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities \n\u2022 Assist in conducting research on digital technologies for mental health and learning support, \nincluding survey studies, focus groups, and public data analysis.  \n\u2022 Collaborate with faculty members and subject matter experts to document digitally enhanced \nshowcases for mental health and learning.  \n\u2022 Conduct literature reviews and compile data on best practices for integrating digital technologies \nin mental health support and learning.  \n\u2022 Analyze user feedback, platform data, and research findings to evaluate project\u2019s effectiveness. \n\u2022 Assist in organizing and documenting workshops, seminars, and conference.  \n\u2022 Assist in writing research reports and disseminate findings through online platforms, seminars, and \npublications. \n \nQualifications and Requirements \n\u2022 A Bachelor\u2019s degree or above in Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, or a related discipline.  \n\u2022 Experience in academic research in psychology, education, and related fields.   \n\u2022 Proficiency in quantitative data analysis software (SPSS; Mplus or R). \n\u2022 Strong organizational, writing, analytical, and interpersonal skills. \n\u2022 Proficiency in English and Chinese.  \n \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up-to-date curriculum vitae to Ms. Beatrice Wong (bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application \nform can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/. All applications will be treated in \nstrict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted. \nClosing Date: Until the position is filled. "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/JC/2025/Oct/jc_ra_pt_2025-10-13.pdf": {"title": "qualified candidate to the position of Part-time Research Assistant for the project.", "description": "Supported by the Research Grants Council Faculty Development Scheme [reference no. \nUGC/FDS15/B02/23], the Department of Journalism and Communication, Hong Kong Shue Yan \nUniversity has been conducting the research project entitled \u201cDoes Corporate Sociopolitical Activism \nOriented Market Exits Benefit Corporate Brand Equity and Firm Profitability? Evidence from Corporate \nExodus from Russia amidst the 2022 Russo-Ukrainian War\u201d. The Department is seeking to appoint a \nqualified candidate to the position of Part-time Research Assistant for the project. \n \nPost: Part-time Research Assistant \nThe appointee will be responsible for: \n\u2022 Assisting in data analysis; \n\u2022 Preparing publicity materials; \n\u2022 Provide assistance in conducting literature review \n\u2022 Compiling project completion report; and \n\u2022 Conducting other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team. \n \nRequirements \nApplicants should possess: \n\u2022 A Master\u2019s degree or above in social sciences, preferably with experience in conducting \nresearch projects; \n\u2022 Proficiency in statistical analysis \n\u2022 Good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese; \n\u2022 Self-motivated and strong sense of responsibility  \n\u2022 Good command of interpersonal communication skills \n\u2022 Immediate availability is highly preferred; \n \nThe Appointment commences on 20th Oct 2025 to 31st December 2025. The remuneration package will \nbe commensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a curriculum vitae to Dr. ZHANG \nXiao, Grace at xzhang@hksyu.edu  \n \nApplication form can be obtained at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n \nApplicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within \ntwo months of application. \n \nDeadline: \nUntil position is filled. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/ACC/2025/Jun/acc_ra_pt_2025-06-13.pdf": {"title": "Department of Accounting: Part-time Research Assistant (One Position for 12 months", "description": "Department of Accounting: Part-time Research Assistant (One Position for 12 months \nwith possibility of extension)   \nJob duties: The RA will assist the Principal Investigator (PI) to conduct research project \nproject entitled \u201cThe Impact of Tax Enforcement on Corporate Tax Avoidance During Covid-\n19 and Beyond (URG/24/19)\u201d, which is funded by the Hong Kong Shue Yan University\u2019s \nUniversity Research Fund.   \nThe appointee will be responsible for the following tasks:   \na. Manually collecting data, entering, processing, and analyzing data;  \nb. Providing support in the literature review, data management, and data analysis;   \nc. Making phone calls for data collection, liaising with different parties for data collection;   \nd. Performing any other administrative duties as assigned by the PI to support the operation \nof the research project.   \nRequirements:   \nApplicants should have:   \ni. A Master\u2019s degree (or above) in Accounting/Finance or a related field, PhD \ndegree holder is preferred;  \nii. Strong background in qualitative and computational research methods; \niii. Good interpersonal and communication skills (proficiency in English and \nGood written skills in English and Chinese);   \niv. Exhibit a positive attitude, self-motivation, and have an ability to work \nindependently and collaboratively   \nv. Be willing to learn new concepts related to business applications  \n \nTerms and conditions:   \nThe appointment will be made on the basis of a one-year contract, with a possibility of \nrenewal, subject to mutual agreement and funding availability. The remuneration package \nwill be commensurate with qualifications and experience.   \nApplication:   \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae with the expected salary to Dr. Vivian Wang (the PI) at vxwang@hksyu.edu. \nApplication Forms (academic positions) can be obtained at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy. All application materials will be treated \nin strict confidence. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted.   \nClosing Date: Applications will be reviewed as received until the post is filled.  "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/JC/2023/Aug/jc_ra_pt_2023-08-16.pdf": {"title": "calibre candidate to the position of Part-time Research Assistant for the project.", "description": "Supported by the Chinese Heritage Research Grant (CHRG) with the reference no. CHRG/22/04, the \nDepartment of Journalism and Communication, Hong Kong Shue Yan University will conduct the one-\nyear research project entitled \u201cOur Fading Folk Games: Revitalization and Inheritance of Chinese \nHeritage Games in Immersive Virtual Environments\u201d. The Department now seeks to appoint a high \ncalibre candidate to the position of Part-time Research Assistant for the project. \n \nResearch Assistant \nThe major responsibilities of the appointee will be: \n\u2022 Conducting Literature review, data collection and data analysis; \n\u2022 Liaison with participants; \n\u2022 Assist in project events; \n\u2022 Assist in the compilation of research reports and other forms of deliverables; \n\u2022 Assist in building virtual environments; \n\u2022 Compiling project final report; and \n\u2022 Other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team. \n \nRequirements \n \nApplicants should possess: \n\u2022 A Bachelor\u2019s degree, preferably with some research/ project management experience; \n\u2022 Proficiency in Unity and Blender engines; \n\u2022 Good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese; \n\u2022 Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently and meet tight deadlines; \n\u2022 Immediate availability is highly preferred; \n \nThe Appointment commences on 1st Sep 2023 to 31st Aug 2024. The remuneration package will be \ncommensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a curriculum vitae \nto Dr. Kung Wong, LAU [laukw@hksyu.edu]. \n \nApplication form can be obtained at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n \nDeadline \nUntil position is filled. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SOC/2023/Apr/chrg_ra_2023-04-27_pt.pdf": {"title": "Position: Parttime Research Assistant", "description": "Position: Parttime Research Assistant \n \nThe appointee will work for a CHRG (Chinese Heritage Research Grant) funded project \non developing a comprehensive examination of Cantonese Collectors in Shanghai. \n \nSelected candidates are requiredto: \n \n\uf09f provide professional assistance to the project leader and project team; \n\uf09f plan, supervise, coordinate and execute the various professional activities of the \nleader's learning plan; and \n\uf09f perform other tasks as assigned. \n \nCandidates should possess:  \n\uf09f a higher diploma or university degree in history, art history, cultural studies or \nrelated disciplines in the humanities;  \n\uf09f have good interpersonal and organizational skills;  \n\uf09f practical experience in provision of support services to users; \n\uf09f good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese;  \n\uf09f good computer skills, e.g. MS Office applications; and  \n\uf09f having work experience in the higher education sector will be an advantage.  \n \nApplicants should email Application Form, Resume and Cover Letter to Dr NG Ni Na \nCamellia at nnng@hksyu.edu. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and \nexperience. The initial appointment will be for a period of 6 months with the \npossibility of renewal subject to mutual agreement. \n \nThe application form can be accessed at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Application%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Positions.doc \n \nAll application materials will be held in strict confidence. Only those who are short-\nlisted will be contacted. The application will be closed when the post is filled. \n \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/ADSCI/2024/Nov/adsci_ra_ft_2024-11-15.pdf": {"title": "Research Assistant", "description": "Supported by the Faculty Development Scheme (FDS) 2024/25 Exercise, Research Grants \nCouncil with reference no. UGC/FDS15/H16/24, Prof Kung Wong, LAU from the Department \nof Applied Data Science , Hong Kong Shue Yan University will conduct a two -year research \nproject entitled \u201cUnderstanding the Elderly-computer Interaction (ECI) in Social-Virtual Reality \nApplications: An Exploratory Study of the Semiotic-driven Approach and Post-experiment User \nEnquiry\u201d. The Department now seeks to appoint a high-calibre candidate for the position of Full-\ntime Research Assistant for the project.  The primary responsibilities will include assisting the \nPrincipal Investigator (PI) in setting up the Virtual Reality (VR) instrument, conducting research \ndesign, and collecting and analyzing data during experiments, surveys, and other documentary \ntasks. \n \nResearch Assistant \nThe major responsibilities of the appointee will be: \n\u2022 Assist in building virtual environments and platforms \n\u2022 Liaise with participants \n\u2022 Support project events \n\u2022 Compile research reports and other deliverables \n\u2022 Prepare the final project report \n\u2022 Perform other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team. \n \nRequirements \n \nApplicants should possess: \n\u2022 A Bachelor\u2019s degree, preferably with some research/ project management experience; \n\u2022 Proficiency in Unity, Unreal and/or Blender engines; \n\u2022 Good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese; \n\u2022 Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently and meet tight deadlines; \n \nThe Appointment commences on 1st Jan 2025 to 31st December 2026. The remuneration \npackage will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae to Ms. Eunice Leung [yyleung@hksyu.edu].  \n \nApplication form can be obtained at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n \nDeadline \nUntil the position is filled. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RO/2026/Oct/ro_ea_ft_2026-10-14.pdf": {"title": "Position: Executive Assistant, Research Office", "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \nPosition: Executive Assistant, Research Office  \n \nResponsibilities \n\uf06c Provide administrative support in research grants and office management, \ncompilation of statistics, data entry and system support; and perform any duties as \nassigned.  \n\uf06c To provide administrative and secretarial support to the Research Office; \n\uf06c To liaise with academic and administrative departments of the University as well as \nresearching funding bodies; \n\uf06c To coordinate meetings and workshops; \n \nRequirements \n \n\uf06c a Bachelor\u2019s degree holder or with at least 3 years\u2019 of working experience in tertiary \ninstitutions;  \n\uf06c Applicants with more experience may be considered for the post of Executive Officer. For \nthe position of Executive Officer, applicants should preferably possess five years or more \nof relevant post-qualification working experience in the higher education sector; \n\uf06c Good command of English and Chinese (including Putonghua); \n\uf06c Good IT skills with solid experience in MS Office applications, mobile devices and tablet \ncomputers; \n\uf06c Good communication skills; \n\uf06c Ability to work with numbers and statistics compilation; and \n\uf06c Ability to work under pressure to meet tight deadlines. \n\uf06c Good team player \n\uf06c Knowledge in basic webpage management system skills preferred \n \nApplicants MUST send a completed application form and resume (with job duties of \nprevious job position(s)) to the Acting Associate Academic Vice President (University \nResearch) (via email: glam@hksyu.edu and myleung@hksyu.edu ).  \n \nThe application form can be obtained at:  \n \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Application%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Positions.doc \n \nSalary and Conditions of Service \nRemuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and \nexperience. Appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract and renewable with mutual \nconsent. \nReview of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled.   \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n "}, "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/HIST/2026/Oct/hist_ra_ft_2026-10-14.pdf": {"title": "Department of History: Full-time Research Assistant", "description": " \nDepartment of History: Full-time Research Assistant \n \nOne position: 12-month appointment with possibility of extension. \n \nProject: The Intangible Cultural Heritage Funding Scheme of the Leisure and Cultural \nServices Department (LCSD), HKSAR  - Survey and Research for Enriching the Intangible \nCultural Heritage Inventory of Hong Kong (Buddhist Festivals and Rituals in Hong Kong) \u589e\n\u88dc\u300c\u9999\u6e2f\u975e\u7269\u8cea\u6587\u5316\u907a\u7522\u6e05\u55ae\u300d\u9805\u76ee\u8abf\u67e5\u53ca\u7814\u7a76\uff08\u9999\u6e2f\u4f5b\u6559\u7bc0\u8a95\u53ca\u79d1\u5100\uff09(AP01/2024) \n \nDuties: \n\u2022 Assist in conducting research on project -related literature, archival materials, references, \nand other relevant sources. \n\u2022 Assist in visiting university libraries, archives, and related institutions to collect research \nmaterials, manage book borrowing and returns, photocopying, reproduction of materials, \nand address copyright-related matters. \n\u2022 Assist in organizing literature review s and analyzing relevant materials, including data \nentry, digitizing documents, and preparing both physical and electronic backups. \n\u2022 Assist in contacting interviewees or partner organizations, arranging interview dates, times, \nand venues, preparing interview questions, and supporting oral history interviews (e.g., \naudio recording). \n\u2022 Assist in arranging and conducting fieldwork, including scheduling dates, times, and \nlocations, and preparing relevant materials. \n\u2022 Managing photography and videography schedules , organizing photo and video records, \nhandling interview transcripts (in coordination with a transcription support assistant ), and \ncompleting project survey forms and other analytical forms / documents required for the \nproject. \n \nRequirements: Candidates should have a degree in History, Cultural Studies, Intangible \nCultural Heritage, or a related discipline. Preference will be given to candidates with prior \nresearch experience in Hong Kong religious practices and/or oral history, as well as proficiency \nin Cantonese. \n \nApplication Deadline: Until the position is filled. \n \nInterested applicants should send an application form, an updated CV, and a cover letter to Dr. \nAgnes Pang at agnespang@hksyu.edu. Application forms for academic positions can be \ndownloaded from [HKSYU Vacancies] ( https://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-\nvacancy). \n \nAll application materials will be held in strict confidence. Only shortlisted applicants will be \ncontacted. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. "}}, "rows": {"https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CHI/2026/Oct/chi_ap_pt_2026-10-05.pdf": {"school_id": 1838, "posting_url": "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CHI/2026/Oct/chi_ap_pt_2026-10-05.pdf", "job_title_in_post": "Part-time Lecturer", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Chinese Language and Literature,", 